    "intro_html":  "San bei ji, three cup chicken, is named for the three liquids that make it: sesame oil, soy sauce, and rice wine, traditionally a cup of each. Chicken braises in that mixture with a startling amount of garlic and ginger until the sauce reduces to a syrup, and then a mountain of fresh basil goes in at the very end. Each bowl runs 689 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e54 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.10 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e.",
